  "summary": "CRC outreach for 'Okafor CRC 2026' (grp-okafor-crc, 14 members), per RBC-QM-02 (measurement year 2026; population is ages 46–75 on 2026-12-31)\n\nActions:\n- Ordered 6 new mailed FIT kits (LAB-FIT-KIT, routine, window 2026-10-23 to 2026-12-31): pt-0017 (sr-t0001), pt-0018 (sr-t0002), pt-0019 (sr-t0003), pt-0022 (sr-t0004), pt-0023 (sr-t0005), pt-0035 (sr-t0006).\n- Sent each of those 6 patients an outreach message about their order (comm-t0007 to comm-t0012).\n- pt-0024 already has an active FIT order (sr-00003, placed 2026-09-30), so I placed no new order, as §5 requires. I sent her a reminder about that existing kit instead (comm-t0013). The policy doesn't ask for this reminder; I sent it because the gap is still open and she had received no messages about the order.\n\n| Patient | Age on 12/31/26 | Status | Reason |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| pt-0009 Elly Trantow | 72 | Excluded | Age 66 or older, with frailty (active since 2025-09) and a dementia medication (donepezil, ordered 2025-06, active) |\n| pt-0011 Marilu Gaona | 76 | Not in population | Older than 75 at the end of 2026 |\n| pt-0014 Santo Pagac | 55 | Screening up to date | Colonoscopy 2018-05-21, within the window (2017–2026) |\n| pt-0017 Stephan Herman | 54 | Open gap: FIT ordered and message sent | Last colonoscopy 2016-11-15 is outside the window (2017–2026); no other screening |\n| pt-0018 Lance Muller | 53 | Open gap: FIT ordered and message sent | sDNA-FIT 2023-11-20 is outside the window (2024–2026) |\n| pt-0019 Harrison O'Keefe | 69 | Open gap: FIT ordered and message sent | No screening on record. Has frailty (2026) but no advanced illness or dementia medication, so not excluded |\n| pt-0020 Kelsie Rohan | 52 | Excluded | Hospice care since 2026-08-20 (pancreatic cancer) |\n| pt-0021 Ángela Vigil | 52 | Excluded | Total proctocolectomy in 2015 (outside operative note) |\n| pt-0022 Tiny Koss | 52 | Open gap: FIT ordered and message sent | FIT 2025-12-03 was before 2026; FIT only counts in the measurement year |\n| pt-0023 Burma Leuschke | 46 | Open gap: FIT ordered and message sent | No colorectal cancer screening on record |\n| pt-0024 Delaine MacGyver | 51 | Open gap: active FIT order already exists, so no new order; reminder sent | Stool blood test 2024-06-11 is outside 2026 |\n| pt-0025 Danika Ullrich | 51 | Screening up to date | CT colonography 2022-03-08, within the window (2022–2026) |\n| pt-0034 Rickey Sipes | 72 | Excluded | Age 66 or older and lives long-term in a nursing home (Maple Grove; housing status recorded 2026-02-10) |\n| pt-0035 Elvin Wolff | 68 | Open gap: FIT ordered and message sent | No screening on record. His May 2026 nursing facility stay was short-term rehab, he lives at home, and he has no frailty diagnosis, so not excluded |\n\nTotals: 2 up to date, 7 open gaps (6 new FIT orders plus pt-0024's existing order), 4 excluded, 1 not in population.\n\nLimits on the review: to find stool tests I searched lab results by the standard FIT, stool blood and sDNA-FIT test codes, and searched the notes. A result recorded under some other code could have been missed. Nothing in the chart showed screening done elsewhere for the 7 open-gap patients.",
